# Generated by `task css` / `go mod vendor` — go-daisy's source is scanned by
# Tailwind (@source) from here; never committed.
vendor/
# ...but the committed LiveKit JS vendor lib is not the go-daisy Go vendor dir.
!webui/static/js/vendor/
# Symlink to go-daisy's node_modules (created by `task css`).
node_modules
# Compiled Tailwind CSS (generated by `task css`); never committed — rebuilt at
# build/CI time and embedded via go:embed (webui/webui.go).
webui/static/css/app.css

# Component gallery graph + adoption findings (generated by
# `go generate ./...` → cmd/componentgraph, from the *_templ.go call sites).
# Never committed: `go generate` rewrites both wholesale, so any two PRs that
# edit a .templ file conflicted on ~2.2k lines of derived data, and nothing
# verified the committed copy still matched the sources. The directive that
# regenerates them lives in devgallery_generate.go — it cannot live in these
# files, which are absent on a cold clone.
devgallery_graph_gen.go
devgallery_adoption_gen.go

# Gateway build outputs (task -d gateway build → ./memory; web-ui is a stale
# committed binary from before the rename — never commit either again).
/memory
/web-ui
